## Deviations
- **Continuation round trip:** a captured continuation cannot be lifted; `lift-slice` refuses it as `:non-canonicalizable` regardless of contents. So the continuation is tested for admission and payload bytes only; the closure does the full lift-and-lower round trip on all four VMs.
- **Snapshot round trip:** there is no dedicated snapshot test. Snapshots are covered through the heap trace, the decoded-program run and the printed output; name the snapshot API if you want a direct test.

